# Forms

- One Zod schema per form in `src/features/<domain>/*-schema.ts`.
- Infer values with `z.infer<typeof schema>`. Do not duplicate hand-written form types.
- Use `useForm` + `zodResolver` from `src/lib/zod-resolver.ts`. Mode: `onTouched`.
- Required messages first, then format/length. Trim emails. Use `z.email()` (Zod 4).
- Show `errors.field?.message` on `TextField`. Keep `noValidate` on the `<form>`.
- Do not call the API until `handleSubmit` succeeds.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
if (!email.includes("@")) errors.email = "invalid"

// ✅ GOOD
export const loginSchema = z.object({
  email: z.string().trim().min(1, "Email is required").pipe(z.email("Enter a valid email address")),
})
export type LoginFormValues = z.infer<typeof loginSchema>
```
